# CVE-2026-14257 / GHSA-mh99-v99m-4gvg — brace-expansion DoS (unbounded expansion → OOM).
# The advisory has ONE affected range (<=5.0.7) fixed ONLY in 5.0.8 — no per-major
# backport, so 1.1.16 and 2.1.2 (the maintainer's maintenance-v1/v2 heads, the latest
# of their lines) are flagged with no in-line fix. Forcing those consumers to 5.x breaks
# them: 5.x moved `module.exports = expand` to a named export, so minimatch@3 / glob /
# eslint (which `require('brace-expansion')()` as a function) throw "expand is not a
# function" (verified in CI). Our genuinely-current 5.x path IS bumped to 5.0.8 (see the
# pnpm override). The residual 1.x/2.x are reached only by build/dev tooling (eslint) and
# server-controlled file archiving (exceljs→archiver, glob patterns we author) — never a
# user-controlled brace pattern, so the DoS is not reachable with untrusted input.
# Revisit when minimatch/glob/eslint upstream adopt brace-expansion@5-native.
CVE-2026-14257

# CVE-2025-71329 + CVE-2025-71330 — image-size@1.2.1 DoS via crafted image buffer.
# NO fixed version exists upstream (both advisories: affected, Fixed Version empty).
# Sole consumer is metro (the React Native bundler inside expo's toolchain): image
# sizing runs at BUNDLE time over repo-authored assets on our own build machines —
# production never feeds untrusted images through metro, so the DoS is not reachable
# with attacker-controlled input. Added 2026-08-17; revisit when metro ships a fixed
# image-size (check `pnpm why image-size` after expo/metro upgrades).
CVE-2025-71329
CVE-2025-71330

# CVE-2026-40345 — deepmerge-ts@7.1.5 stack exhaustion on recursive object graphs
# (fixed in 8.0.0). Sole dependency path: @prisma/config@6.19.2 — Prisma's own CLI
# config tooling, which merges OUR checked-in config during `prisma generate`/
# `migrate`, never attacker-controlled recursive objects, and never at app runtime.
# Forcing a transitive MAJOR under Prisma's CLI risks breaking codegen for an
# unreachable vuln. Added 2026-08-18; drop when Prisma bumps its own dependency
# (check `pnpm why deepmerge-ts` after Prisma upgrades).
CVE-2026-40345
